 "section_summary": "This section contains the concluding portion (pages iii–vi and 1–59) of a comprehensive SCAP Civil Information and Education Section survey report on educational institutions in Tottori Prefecture, Japan, in 1946. It provides an introductory overview of the Japanese educational administration across national, public, and private control jurisdictions, followed by detailed summary statistical tables showing student enrollment and faculty numbers as of April 30 and November 30, 1946. The bulk of the section is an exhaustive institutional roster documenting higher, secondary, elementary, vocational, and special schools throughout Tottori Prefecture's cities, towns, and villages. The report concludes with an outline reference map of the Chugoku region displaying prefectural capitals, population centers over 100,000, and higher educational institutions.",
 "subfiles": [
