   "start_page": 237,
   "summary": "This survey report details the structure, statistics, and individual institutions of the educational system in Tottori Prefecture in 1946. It outlines the scope of national, prefectural, municipal, village/town, and private educational control, noting the cooperative data-gathering effort between SCAP's Civil Information and Education Section and the Japanese Ministry of Education. Statistical summary tables compile institution numbers, teacher counts, and student enrollments as of April 30 and November 30, 1946, across higher, secondary, elementary, and special education levels. The extensive roster catalogues every individual school and kindergarten by locality, recording founding dates, sex of students, enrollment, and teaching personnel, and concludes with a regional map of the Chugoku district.",
   "title": "Japanese Educational Institutions by Control Jurisdiction, Level, and Type: Tottori Prefecture",
